    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change returns `contactPreference = \"EMAIL\"` when an owner has an email, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`, exposed on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe project derives read-only response fields (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `displayName`) as `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` entity, which MapStruct maps into the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`. I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field, and MapStruct wires it automatically by name).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` returning `\"EMAIL\"` when `email` is present/non-blank, else `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nNo OfficeFloor YAML or function changes were needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwner` step already serializes the mapped DTO. Both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.",
