        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `getContactPreference()` getter fits the codebase's established idiom exactly. `Owner` already hosts a family of `@Transient` derived getters (`getMembershipLevel()`, `getLocality()`) that compute presentation/derived values from the owner's own fields, each with the same Javadoc convention (\"Derived from the owner's own fields.\"). The new method:\n\n- Lives in the right unit \u2014 a self-contained derivation on the entity it depends on, not smeared across a service or mapper.\n- Reuses the exact `hasEmail` idiom already present in `getMembershipLevel()` (line 185), so it reads as native to the class rather than introducing a competing style.\n- Is not duplicated anywhere, and doesn't turn `Owner` into a catch-all \u2014 it's one more small sibling in an existing, coherent group.\n- Is documented in `openapi.yml` alongside the other derived, `readOnly` fields, matching their title/description/example shape.\n\nNo structural improvements needed."
